DIGITAL ESTATE PLANNING CHECKLIST

STEP 1: MAKE AN INVENTORY
□ List all email accounts
□ List all financial accounts (banks, investments, PayPal, crypto)
□ List all social media accounts
□ List all cloud storage accounts
□ List all shopping accounts
□ List all subscriptions
□ List all travel/loyalty programs
□ List all healthcare portals
□ List all government accounts
□ List all smart home devices and apps
□ List all AI service accounts
□ List all devices (phones, tablets, computers)
□ List all domain names and websites

STEP 2: CHOOSE A DIGITAL EXECUTOR
□ Select a trustworthy, tech-comfortable person
□ Have the conversation about responsibilities
□ Give them access to credentials (password manager emergency contact, sealed document, or safe)
□ Make sure they can unlock your phone and computer
□ Name a backup executor

STEP 3: SECURE YOUR CREDENTIALS
□ Set up a password manager (Bitwarden, 1Password, NordPass, or Proton Pass)
□ Migrate away from LastPass if currently using it
□ Document passkey locations and backup methods
□ Enable emergency access in your password manager
□ Consider a printed backup in a fireproof safe

STEP 4: SET UP PLATFORM LEGACY FEATURES
□ Google: Enable Inactive Account Manager
□ Apple: Add Legacy Contact and share access key
□ Facebook: Set memorialization preferences and legacy contact
□ Microsoft: Document Next of Kin process for executor
□ X (Twitter): Plan for deactivation (no reliable legacy feature)
□ LinkedIn: Document closure process
□ Instagram: Document memorialization process

STEP 5: PUT IT IN YOUR WILL
□ Name digital executor explicitly
□ Reference inventory location
□ Specify wishes for social media (memorialize vs. delete)
□ Specify wishes for domain names and websites
□ Grant authority to access and close accounts
□ Review with estate attorney

ONGOING
□ Review inventory every 6-12 months
□ Update after major life changes
□ Update when adding new devices or accounts
